    about: `Launched in 2023, the One-Year Part-Time Diploma in Kuchipudi is a flagship cultural initiative of Adikavi Nannaya University. Designed for passionate women students and aspiring women artists across the East Godavari and West Godavari districts, the program aims to preserve, nurture, and propagate the rich heritage of classical Kuchipudi dance.

The curriculum seamlessly blends intensive practical training with in-depth theoretical study, transforming aspiring dancers into accomplished performers. Students in this program form the cultural heartbeat of the campus, actively participating and performing in all major university events, festivals, and official celebrations.

The program has witnessed rapid growth and strong community demand since its inception.

First Batch: Successfully completed with an intake of 20 + 2 students.

Second Batch: Successfully completed with an intake of 20 + 2 students.

Third Batch (Current): Capacity expanded to 40 + 4 students, with 37 seats filled by talented upcoming artistes.

To accommodate regular academics and working individuals, the course is structured as an accessible evening program.

Course Mode: Evening Part-Time Course

Class Timings: 4:30 PM to 7:30 PM

Frequency: Thrice a week – 3 days per week.

The course focuses on mastering classical Kuchipudi adavus, mudras, abhinaya, and traditional repertoire items. Students also receive vibrant opportunities to showcase their talent on official university platforms and regional cultural stages.

The practical and professional structure of the course has yielded excellent career outcomes for graduates. Alumni from the first and second batches have successfully established independent dance academies and cultural institutions. Graduates have also secured prestigious positions as dance educators and cultural instructors in renowned international schools, paving the way for sustainable careers in performing arts.`,

